  "metadata": {
    "title": "[SYNTHETIC FIXTURE] CO adsorption sites on Pt(111) at low coverage from IRRAS and XPS",
    "authors": [],
    "doi": null,
    "year": null,
    "summary": "Synthetic fixture for pipeline testing, not a real publication: a study of the adsorption sites of CO on Pt(111) at 0.25 ML coverage and 300 K using XRD, LEED, IRRAS and XPS. A p(2x2) LEED pattern is observed at 0.25 ML, IRRAS shows a strong C-O stretching band at 2090 cm-1 and a weak band at 1850 cm-1, and C 1s XPS shows a main component at 286.8 eV and a minor component at 286.1 eV. The authors assign the 2090 cm-1 band to CO bound atop a single Pt atom and the 1850 cm-1 band to bridge-bonded CO, and conclude that atop CO is the majority species at 0.25 ML and bridge CO a minority species. The ratio of atop to bridge CO is not quantified, and whether hollow sites are occupied is not addressed. Reconstruction target: CO adsorbed on a Pt(111) slab at 0.25 ML."
  },
